 | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: sum of shipment.quantity where status != CANCELLED for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.delivered | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: sum of shipment.quantity where status = DELIVERED for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.status | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: DELIVERED if delivered==quantity; FULLY_ALLOCATED if allocated==quantity; PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED if allocated&gt;0 and &lt;quantity; UNALLOCATED if allocated==0 |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&amp;limit=L&amp;offset=O | orders (list) | Stored | Order entities (with computed fulfilment for each) |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&amp;limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | OrderController.list(): count of orders matching fulfilment filter before pagination |\n| GET /orders?limit=L&amp;offset=O | orders without filter | Stored | Order entities (with computed fulfilment) |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | orderId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | carrier | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | status | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | quantity | Stored | Shipment entity field (new) |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&amp;offset=O | shipments (list) | Stored | Shipment entities |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | ShipmentController.list(): total count of all shipments |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | name | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | email | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&amp;offset=O | customers (list) | Stored | Customer entities |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | CustomerController.list(): total count of all customers |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | quantity | Stored | Order entity (newly set) |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | fulfilment | Computed | OrderController: recalculated based on new quantity and existing shipments |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CONFIRMED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to DELIVERED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CANCELLED) |\n\n### Shape\n\nOrder fulfilment is a computed read model nested within order responses that aggregates shipment state: allocated and delivered are sums of shipment quantities (filtered by shipment status), status is derived from these sums relative to the order's quantity, and all three are recomputed on every read from the shipments table for the order. Pagination is applied uniformly across list endpoints (orders, shipments, customers) via limit and offset parameters with a total count before pagination in the X-Total-Count response header.\n\n### Unresolved\n\n**None.** All read paths map to either direct entity storage or computed aggregations:\n- All entity fields (customerId, orderId, quantity, status, carrier, etc.) exist as stored data in the in-memory repositories\n- All computed values (fulfilment.allocated, fulfilment.delivered, fulfilment.status, X-Total-Count) are aggregations or derived values that would be computed at read time by the controller or service layer based on repository queries\n- Query parameters (limit, offset, fulfilment) are passed to controllers and determine which rows are fetched and how fulfilment status filtering is applied before pagination\n\nThe task is well-scoped: all referenced values can be traced to either existing entity fields (or new fields like quantity on Order and Shipment), or straightforward computations (sums and comparisons) that aggregate across shipments for an order.\n\n**Relevant file paths:**\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/Customer.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt`","uuid":"57c1e0dc-f1c4-45cd-b53a-b3296fb85eb7","session_id":"ed641a0f-949a-40cd-8812-cb41c2b69a72"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N1MS5EhS1bpKfW7NuxtfdT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: affcf5b152f36e071 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'affcf5b152f36e071', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-jr-lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn-T-observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/ed641a0f-949a-40cd-8812-cb41c2b69a72/tasks/affcf5b152f36e071.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed641a0f-949a-40cd-8812-cb41c2b69a72","uuid":"f609dcea-1c92-4cdf-bf87-ca9490b2eb62","timestamp":"2026-09-25T13:02:34.562Z","tool_use_result":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"affcf5b152f36e071","description":"Implement BE-005 ticket","resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","prompt":"BE-005 — Partial fulfilment, customer check, paged lists\n\nThree changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n## Notes for the agent\n\nThe service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\nverify your work before finishing.\n\n---\n\n## PLANNER HANDOFF\n\n### Analysis: BE-005 Read Paths and Value Storage\n\nBased on my reading of the repository, here is the table of all read paths mentioned in the ticket:\n\n### Read Paths\n\n| Read Path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where Computed |\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | orderId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | customerId | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | amount | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | currency | Stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | quantity | Stored | Order entity field (new) |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.allocated | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: sum of shipment.quantity where status != CANCELLED for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.delivered | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: sum of shipment.quantity where status = DELIVERED for this order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.status | Computed | OrderController/OrderService: DELIVERED if delivered==quantity; FULLY_ALLOCATED if allocated==quantity; PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED if allocated&gt;0 and &lt;quantity; UNALLOCATED if allocated==0 |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&amp;limit=L&amp;offset=O | orders (list) | Stored | Order entities (with computed fulfilment for each) |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&amp;limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | OrderController.list(): count of orders matching fulfilment filter before pagination |\n| GET /orders?limit=L&amp;offset=O | orders without filter | Stored | Order entities (with computed fulfilment) |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | orderId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | carrier | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | status | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | quantity | Stored | Shipment entity field (new) |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&amp;offset=O | shipments (list) | Stored | Shipment entities |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | ShipmentController.list(): total count of all shipments |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | name | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | email | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&amp;offset=O | customers (list) | Stored | Customer entities |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&amp;offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | CustomerController.list(): total count of all customers |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | quantity | Stored | Order entity (newly set) |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | fulfilment | Computed | OrderController: recalculated based on new quantity and existing shipments |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CONFIRMED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to DELIVERED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CANCELLED) |\n\n### Shape\n\nOrder fulfilment is a computed read model nested within order responses that aggregates shipment state: allocated and delivered are sums of shipment quantities (filtered by shipment status), status is derived from these sums relative to the order's quantity, and all three are recomputed on every read from the shipments table for the order. Pagination is applied uniformly across list endpoints (orders, shipments, customers) via limit and offset parameters with a total count before pagination in the X-Total-Count response header.\n\n### Unresolved\n\n**None.** All read paths map to either direct entity storage or computed aggregations:\n- All entity fields (customerId, orderId, quantity, status, carrier, etc.) exist as stored data in the in-memory repositories\n- All computed values (fulfilment.allocated, fulfilment.delivered, fulfilment.status, X-Total-Count) are aggregations or derived values that would be computed at read time by the controller or service layer based on repository queries\n- Query parameters (limit, offset, fulfilment) are passed to controllers and determine which rows are fetched and how fulfilment status filtering is applied before pagination\n\nThe task is well-scoped: all referenced values can be traced to either existing entity fields (or new fields like quantity on Order and Shipment), or straightforward computations (sums and comparisons) that aggregate across shipments for an order.\n\n**Relevant file paths:**\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/Customer.kt`\n- `/private/var/folders/jr/lwz