sent)\n\n## Failing Tests\n\nNone. All 40 tests pass.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Command:** `cd /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-275d4cac-f43b-479d-bd46-ebb136e18e57/sample-service &amp;&amp; ./mvnw test`\n\n**Result:** \n```\nTests run: 40, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nAll 40 tests pass. The uncovered rows are specifically the fulfilment filter feature (`GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS`), which the ticket explicitly requires but has no test. The test suite also does not fully exercise all fulfilment statuses (FULLY_ALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED) or the cancellation-release scenario mentioned in the ticket's acceptance criteria.\n\n---\n\n## BOUNCE REQUEST\n\nThe verifier identified the following uncovered test cases that are required by the ticket:\n\n**Uncovered rows:**\n1. GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&limit=L&offset=O | orders (list) — no test for fulfilment filter parameter\n2. GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&limit=L&offset=O | X-Total-Count header — no test for X-Total-Count with fulfilment filter\n\n**Additional test gaps (acceptance criteria from ticket):**\n1. Fulfilment status FULLY_ALLOCATED (only UNALLOCATED tested)\n2. Fulfilment status PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED (not tested)\n3. Fulfilment status DELIVERED (order's fulfilment.status after delivery not verified)\n4. Release of cancelled shipment's quantity (cancellation tested but effect on fulfilment.allocated not verified)\n5. Fulfilment recalculation after quantity amendment with existing shipments (tested only without shipments)\n\nPlease add tests to cover these scenarios:\n- Test `GET /orders?fulfilment=UNALLOCATED` returns only UNALLOCATED orders\n- Test `GET /orders?fulfilment=FULLY_ALLOCATED` with shipments that fully allocate\n- Test `GET /orders?fulfilment=PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` with partial shipments\n- Test `GET /orders?fulfilment=DELIVERED` with delivered shipments\n- Test X-Total-Count header reflects total after fulfilment 