 fulfilment for each) |\n| GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS&limit=L&offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | OrderController.list(): count of orders matching fulfilment filter before pagination |\n| GET /orders?limit=L&offset=O | orders without filter | Stored | Order entities (with computed fulfilment) |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | orderId | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | carrier | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | status | Stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | quantity | Stored | Shipment entity field (new) |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&offset=O | shipments (list) | Stored | Shipment entities |\n| GET /shipments?limit=L&offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | ShipmentController.list(): total count of all shipments |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | name | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | email | Stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&offset=O | customers (list) | Stored | Customer entities |\n| GET /customers?limit=L&offset=O | X-Total-Count header | Computed | CustomerController.list(): total count of all customers |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | quantity | Stored | Order entity (newly set) |\n| POST /orders/{orderId}/quantity response | fulfilment | Computed | OrderController: recalculated based on new quantity and existing shipments |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CONFIRMED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to DELIVERED) |\n| POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel response | status | Stored | Shipment entity (updated to CANCELLED) |\n\nShape: Order fulfilment is a computed read model nested within order responses that aggregates shipment state: allocated and delivered are sums of shipment quantities (filtered by shipment status), status is derived from these sums relative to the order's quantity, and all three are recomputed on every read from the shipments table for the order. Pagination is applied uniformly across list endpoints (orders, shipments, customers) via limit and offset parameters with a total count before pagination in the X-Total-Count response header.\n\nUnresolved: None.\n\n---\n\n**IMPLEMENTER HANDOFF (FINAL):**\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added quantity field (default 1), fulfilment computed field, FulfilmentStatus enum, UpdateOrderQuantityRequest class\n- Shipment.kt: Added quantity field (default 1), added DELIVERED status to ShipmentStatus enum\n- OrderController.kt: Added customer validation (422), quantity field validation (400), fulfilment computation, list pagination with fulfilment filter, PUT endpoint for quantity update, X-Total-Count header, and fixed fulfilment filtering logic to ensure computed values\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added quantity field validation (400), allocation validation (409), three state transition endpoints (confirm/deliver/cancel), list pagination with X-Total-Count header\n- CustomerController.kt: Changed GET by ID to throw error envelope (404), added list pagination with X-Total-Count header\n- OrderRepository.kt: Added findAll(limit, offset) and count() methods\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findAll(limit, offset), count(), and findByOrderId() methods\n- CustomerRepository.kt: Added findAll(limit, offset), count(), and existsById() methods\n- ApiExceptions.kt: Added UnprocessableEntityException class\n- ApiError.kt: Added error codes: CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND, INVALID_CUSTOMER, ALLOCATION_CONFLICT, INVALID_TRANSITION\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Updated to create customers before orders, added 14 new tests covering quantity, customer validation, fulfilment statuses (UNALLOCATED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED), pagination, fulfilment filtering, quantity amendments, cancelled shipment quantity release, and parameter validation\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Updated to create customers/orders before shipments, added 10 new tests\n- CustomerControllerTest.kt: Added 4 new tests\n\nTests (49 total):\n- OrderControllerTest: 24 tests (filters by all four fulfilment statuses, X-Total-Count with filter, invalid parameter validation, cancelled shipment release, quantity amendment with shipments)\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 17 tests\n- CustomerControllerTest: 7 tests\n- SampleServiceApplicationTests: 1 test\n\nVerification: BUILD SUCCESS — Tests run: 49, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n\nNot Done: Nothing.\n\n---\n\n**VERIFIER FINAL REPORT:**\n\nAll 49 tests pass. Coverage mapping confirms all 27 read paths from planner's table are exercised by tests:\n\n- GET /orders/{orderId} quantity, fulfilment.allocated, fulfilment.delivered, fulfilment.status — Covered\n- GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS filtered list, X-Total-Count with filter — Covered by `filters orders by UNALLOCATED/FULLY_ALLOCATED/PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED/DELIVERED` and `returns X-Total-Count header in list response with fulfilment filter`\n- GET /orders?limit=L&offset=O unpaged list — Covered by `lists orders with pagination`\n- GET /shipments/{shipmentId} quantity, status — Covered\n- POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm/deliver/cancel — Covered\n- Cancelled shipment releases quantity — Covered by `cancels a shipment and releases its quantity`\n- PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity quantity and fulfilment — Covered by `amends order quantity and recalculates fulfilment with existing shipments`\n- GET /customers, GET /shipments pagination and X-Total-Count — Covered\n- Customer validation (422), unknown customer (404 error envelope) — Covered\n- Invalid fulfilment parameter (400) — Covered by `returns 400 for invalid fulfilment parameter`\n\nRows uncovered: None.\n\nFailing tests: None.\n\nBuild: SUCCESS\n\n---\n\n### Bounced\n\nYes. The first verifier run identified 2 uncovered rows (GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS filtered list and X-Total-Count with filter) and 5 test gaps (FULLY_ALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED fulfilment statuses; cancelled shipment quantity release; quantity amendment with existing shipments). The implementer added 9 new tests to cover these gaps.\n\n### Not Done\n\nNothing. All ticket requirements are implemented and tested:\n\n1. ✓ Partial fulfilment: quantity fields, allocation validation, three shipment transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), fulfilment status computation (UNALLOCATED/PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED/FULLY_ALLOCATED/DELIVERED)\n2. ✓ Customer validation: POST /orders rejects unknown customer with 422; GET /customers/{customerId} unknown customer returns 404 through error envelope\n3. ✓ Paged lists: GET /customers, GET /orders, GET /shipments accept limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (0+, default 0); all reject invalid parameters with 400; all return X-Total-Count header; GET /orders respects fulfilment filter before pagination\n4. ✓ Cancelled shipment releases quantity and recalculates order fulfilment\n5. ✓ Order quantity amendment after shipments exist, with fulfilment recalculation and allocation conflict validation\n6. ✓ No new Maven dependencies added\n7. ✓ No unrelated production file changes (only order, shipment, customer features and shared api package modified)","ttft_ms":3096,"type":"result","duration_ms":25855,"uuid":"7bf0ca64-a897-43a1-bb63-7ee94a88ff4f","ttft_stream_ms":979,"time_to_request_ms":15,"first_content_frame_ms":979,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":5}

